      "qty": 12,
      "pos": [
        -16.0,
        0.2,
        -2.5
      ]
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "scout_journal",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "assets/models/props/lectern_ledger.glb",
      "pos": [
        -19.2,
        0.0,
        -2.4
      ],
      "rot_y": 120.0,
      "prompt": "Read Kaelen's Field Journal",
      "title": "Field Journal of Kaelen, Ashbound",
      "text": "Day 41. The boundary stone of Oakhallow again. Four hundred and twelve souls, it says. I count the foundations in the bracken: none. I count the wells: one, dry, with a bucket still on the rope.\n\nDay 43. The Annex has sunk. Its upper offices fell into something older underneath, and the stairs now go down further than the building ever went up. The skeletons inside still keep office hours.\n\nDay 44. A traveller from Bellwether asked what we Ashbound are for. I told her: somebody has to remember things on purpose."
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "baggy_case_board",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "assets/models/props/lectern_ledger.glb",
      "pos": [
        10.2,
        0.0,
        -6.4
      ],
      "rot_y": -60.0,
      "prompt": "Read Baggy's Case Notes",
      "title": "CASE FILE #1: THE MISSING TOWN",
      "text": "Property of BAGGY, Private Eye (Licence pending. Licence fee also pending.)\n\nSUSPECTS:\n1. The hedge. Too neat. Hiding something.\n2. The Bureau. Too many forms. Hiding EVERYTHING.\n3. A goat. (Probably not involved. Looked at me funny.)\n4. Myself? (Ruled out. I have an alibi: I was here. Wait.)\n\nCLUES:\n- Boundary stone says 412 people. I count 0 people. Discrepancy of 412. Very large discrepancy.\n- One dry well. One bucket. Somebody was thirsty, once.\n- I remember a girl with flour on her nose who gave me a sweet roll. I was seven. Nobody else remembers her. CENTRAL MYSTERY.\n\nTHEORY: A whole town was erased by someone with very good handwriting.\n\nNEXT STEPS: Find the town. Find the girl. Find my other glove."
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "sabrino_stash",
      "type": "chest",
      "model": "assets/models/props/treasure_chest.glb",
      "pos": [
        -12.0,
        0.0,
        12.6
      ],
      "rot_y": 180.0,
      "locked": false,
      "loot_table": "core:loot.crypt_basic",
      "fixed_items": [
        "core:item.sabrino_hat",
        "core:item.tome_sabrino",
        "core:item.mana_potion",
        "core:item.mana_potion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "sabrino_note",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "",
      "pos": [
        -10.4,
        0.95,
        12.4
      ],
      "prompt": "Read the Garlic-Scented Note",
      "title": "A Note, Weighed Down with a Clove of Garlic",
      "text": "To Whoever Finds My Hat,\n\nThe Bureau is onto me again. They have charged me with 1,412 counts of Unlicensed Fireballing, which is a lie. It was 1,413. They always forget the one at the wedding.\n\nI am leaving the hat and my good grimoire here under the pine, because a witch on the run cannot also carry a hat that tall. It keeps catching on tavern doors. Very bad for a dramatic exit.\n\nTake them. Wear the hat crooked, it works better. Cast the fireball from FAR away. Further than that. No, further.\n\nAnd if a nice man in a long coat asks where I went, tell him dinner is at eight, as always, and he is still invited.\n\nCiao,\nSabrino\n\nP.S. Do not let anyone tell you that pineapple goes on anything. That is the real war crime.",
      "quest_id": "core:quest.dinner_at_eight",
      "set_stage": 0,
      "set_flag": "sabrino_in_town"
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "script_page_2",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "",
      "pos": [
        -6.0,
        1.6,
        -8.35
      ],
      "rot_y": 0.0,
      "prompt": "Pick Up the Torn Script Page",
      "title": "THE TRAGEDIE OF THE UNCOUNTED KING - Page Two",
      "text": "ACT TWO, SCENE ONE. A haunted battlement. Moonlight.\n\nPRINCE VALIANT: Spectre! Release the King!\n\nGHOST OF THE OLD KING: Never! For I too was forgotten, and I will not be forgotten alone!\n\nPRINCE VALIANT: Then have at thee!\n\n(They duel. It goes on for some time.)\n\n(It goes on for a bit longer.)\n\n[Margin, red ink: 'These two are clearly in love. The playwright appears to be the only person in the audience who has not noticed. - M.Q.']\n\nThe page has been nailed to a pine tree, at exactly the height of a critic's top hat.",
      "set_flag": "page_2"
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "trout_stone",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "",
      "pos": [
        5.2,
        0.0,
        -4.6
      ],
      "rot_y": 0.0,
      "prompt": "Look Up at the Top of the Stone",
      "title": "On Top of the Boundary Stone",
      "text": "Eleven feet up, on the very top of the boundary stone, where nothing larger than a crow could possibly perch, there is a neat, fresh pile of horse manure.\n\nIt is still steaming.\n\nThere are no hoofprints anywhere round the base of the stone. There are no hoofprints on the stone. There is just the evidence, on top, steaming, defying every law of nature and several of the Bureau's.",
      "set_flag": "trout_c_stone"
    }
